(SECTION: 4. CONTRACT DURATION AND SURVIVAL) '
(This Agreement governs disclosures made within two \(2\) years of the) '
(Effective Date. The confidentiality obligations regarding trade secrets) '
(shall remain in perpetuity, while all other confidential technical) '
(materials shall remain protected for three \(3\) years post-termination.) '
() '
(SECTION: 5. REMEDIES FOR BREACH) '
(The parties acknowledge that unauthorized disclosure or use of Confidential) '
(Information will cause irreparable harm for which monetary damages alone) '
(would be inadequate. Accordingly, the Disclosing Party shall be entitled to) '
(seek injunctive relief and specific performance.) '
() '
(SECTION: 6. GOVERNING LAW) '
(This Mutual Non-Disclosure Agreement shall be governed by and construed) '
(under the laws of the State of New York, United States.) '
() '
